created: 2023-02-03, last updated: 2026-07-23, [Read more](https://qwik.dev/docs/server$/)

When using `server$`, you have access to the `RequestEvent` object through `this`.
This object provides useful information about the HTTP request, including environment variables, cookies, URL, and headers.
Here's how you can use it:
...
### Cookies
You can read cookies using `this.cookie.get()` and `this.cookie.set()`.
> When using `handleCookies` (in our example below) if it's used within a `useTask$` function that runs during the initial request, setting cookies won’t work as expected.
...
If you need to set cookies for the initial document request you can use `plugin@<name>.ts` or Middleware.
